  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "7a0d0e64-18b8-407d-8736-d982a3625767"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a step-by-step view of a scene on a graph"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"d5852890-87be-41f8-b13b-82087ebf056d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Underlying graphs", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"57330d9c-70ea-4e8c-b7ac-1974251fa149"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SprayGraph"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/SprayGraph", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "b5cbf112-1cc3-4819-9979-f9c016397334"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the breadth-first DAG rooted at c, whose source-to-sink paths are exactly \
the maximal shortest paths from c"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"e8b677fb-77dc-40cb-8e65-8994a84d44ff"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Not here", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"753eed7f-7904-4f3d-a8d8-11cd7fea69dc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindBallHull"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindBallHull", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "ba61783d-a4dc-4618-a5ef-f217f5c31701"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the intersection of all balls containing a set of points; it lives on the \
Infra Topology guide"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"acc3a4c5-00f2-4089-b677-acc8d0a16ce3"],

Cell["\<\
not here: the quadric as an inert head and the layers of the convex hull; \
FindInfraQuadric stays on the Experimental guide\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"7754a77b-9aff-4529-9b36-147881cb2256"],

Cell["\<\
not here: an invariant of four points, the inverse of every head (the values \
of its unknowns for a given vertex set), and the graph of a line or of an arc \
as an exported name; none is in an item yet\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"587ae7c0-8588-41f4-aa97-6cc3a74992ae"],

Cell["\<\
not here: the interactive multi-construction stepper in the causal and \
branchial direction; it stays on the Experimental guide\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"264e4564-fe4b-4b5f-b811-b2a98a1e27a0"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

